# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Generated acados solvers. Rebuilt by each variant's
# expert_src/generate_solver_via_acados.py, and NOT portable: acados bakes the
# build-time absolute path into the generated JSON, so a copied solver silently
# loads from wherever it was first built.
**/expert_src/lib/

# Simulation output. Everything under results/ is regenerable by re-running the
# campaigns in src/experiments/simulation/jobs/, so none of it is tracked: raw
# traces and checkpoints, aggregated CSVs, rendered figures and job logs alike.
# results/logs/ is the one exception: the directory itself is tracked via an
# empty .gitkeep, because Slurm does not create a missing --output directory and
# a job whose log file cannot be opened dies at launch. Git cannot re-include a
# path inside an ignored directory, so results/ is ignored by contents (/*)
# rather than as a whole.
src/experiments/simulation/results/*
!src/experiments/simulation/results/logs/
src/experiments/simulation/results/logs/*
!src/experiments/simulation/results/logs/.gitkeep

# Data and rendered media anywhere else in the tree, same reasoning.
*.csv
*.png
*.pdf
*.mp4
*.gif

# Slurm job output, when a job is launched without redirecting to $WORK
*.out
*.err

# Tuning scratch: worker scripts and payloads written at run time by their parent
# driver, plus resumable Optuna study state. The exported CSVs are the record.
_sweep_worker_*.py
_sweep_result_*.json
_timing_worker.py
_timing_result_*.json
**/sweep_results/*.db

# Editor and OS
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store
